  "body": "What happens: the local batch gate on main `4f4edcf35` fails two app tests. The post refuses two legal stock-source cuts.\n\nEvidence (`cargo xtask gate batch`, log `07-app_suites`):\n\n1. `-p camcraft-app --test stock_source_cross_drill`, test `a_stock_source_cross_drill_at_the_modelled_holes_size_is_excused_its_faceted_wall`, `crates/app/tests/stock_source_cross_drill.rs:211`:\n```\nbar turned false: posts: post blocked - stock sim did not judge this program: S1: move 1: posed moves are not modelled by the column engine (its atoms stand upright on +Z; a tilted tool cut upright is a wrong verdict) - and S1 now cuts part 'bar' (move 1 cuts past the finish surface) - a part moved, added or no longer workholding since it was generated; regenerate it\n```\n2. `-p camcraft-app --test stock_source_holes`, test `a_hole_kind_in_the_parts_own_hole_or_in_stock_only_material_posts`, `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes_support/mod.rs:333`:\n```\ndrill-in-hole-true: a legal stock-source cut posts: post blocked - stock sim did not judge this program: the program sim models an axis-aligned stock; this stock carries a rotation - and S1 now cuts part 'part' (move 1 cuts past the finish surface) - a part moved, added or no longer workholding since it was generated; regenerate it\n```\n\nProbable cause (not confirmed): the live judgment of kept parts at the post (PR 1643) does not apply the excuses that the generation-time judgment gives to a stock-source hole cut (PR 1634, PR 1640, PR 1644). A drill in the part's own modelled hole is then reported as a cut into the part.\n\nExpected: the post gives the same verdict as the generation-time judgment for an unchanged document. A real cut into a part must still block the post.\n\nThis holds the v0.20.0 release gate.\n\nDone means: the two tests pass, and a pinning test shows that a stock-source drill which cuts solid part material is still refused at the post.\n",
